{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787080610,"nonce":"HdQAoW0BG0NqQnonnia5HzLhwOU=","title":"`00057`'s header promises the flap columns are live state, and the retirement that made them frozen landed the same day","message":"**What is wrong.** `db/migrations/00057_a_case_outlives_the_flap.sql:83-92` carries a paragraph headed *\"⚠️ `alerts.flap_score` AND `alerts.is_flapping` ARE NOT MADE DEAD BY W AND ARE NOT RETIRED HERE.\"* It goes on: *\"They are the VISIBLE state — 'a VISIBLE UI state, never silent suppression' (00007:50) — that tells an operator to go fix a Prometheus rule missing a `for:`, and the API filter and the rollup both read them.\"* It closes by scoping a follow-up: *\"Feeding the deferred resolve into that score needs a new `alert_events.type`, which is an API-contract change and deliberately not bundled here.\"*\n\nThe paragraph is a promise about what survives the change, and by the end of the same day it did not.\n\n**The demonstration.** ADR 0041 Amendment 1 retired the detector. `internal/alerts/service/sweep.go:740-741` — *\"⭐ WHAT SURVIVES, AND WHY IT IS NOT A CONTRADICTION. `alerts.flap_score` and `alerts.is_flapping` are RETIRED IN PLACE, not dropped.\"* `internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:1214-1215` records that `SetFlap` — *\"the only statement in the tree that ever wrote `alerts.flap_score` OR `alerts.is_flapping`\"* — is deleted. `internal/notification/domain/mode.go:166-177` puts the consequence in the plainest terms: *\"⛔ AND IT IS NO LONGER A LIVE FACT … both columns keep the last value they were given and nothing recomputes them … What a reader gets is a MEASUREMENT TAKEN AT A TIME, not a current judgement.\"*\n\nTwo of the header's three claims fail against that, and the third is voided:\n\n*The columns are not \"VISIBLE state that tells an operator to go fix a Prometheus rule\".* They are a frozen reading of an unspecified past moment. `mode.go:174-177` says why the freezing was correct — *\"the detector was retired because the case retention window W (00057) made it report `false` exactly when an alert was flapping hardest, and a detector that lies is worse than no detector\"* — which is 00057's own change retiring the thing 00057 promised to keep.\n\n*\"The API filter and the rollup both read them\" is still literally true and no longer means what the sentence uses it to mean.* `internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:778` (`?flapping=`) and `:996` (`count(*) FILTER (WHERE is_flapping)`) both still read the columns. A reader of `00057:86` takes that as evidence the columns are live; it is evidence that two surfaces now serve a stale verdict.\n\n*The follow-up is void.* \"Feeding the deferred resolve into that score needs a new `alert_events.type`\" describes work on a score nothing computes. Anyone picking it up from this file would implement an event type to feed a retired EWMA.\n\n**Why it matters.** `00057` is the migration for the case-retention window W, so it is the file a maintainer opens to understand what W did — and its header is emphatic, dated by its own filename, and wrong about the change that immediately followed it. The specific misreading it invites is the expensive one: that `alerts.is_flapping` can be trusted as a current judgement, which is exactly what the retirement decided it cannot be. `mode.go:176-177` already states the only words the column can now support — *\"'the last stored verdict', never 'is flapping now'\"* — and `00057:83-92` states the opposite.\n\n**Where.** `db/migrations/00057_a_case_outlives_the_flap.sql:83-92` (the paragraph) · `docs/adr/0041-*` Amendment 1 and `docs/adr/0042-storm-damping-is-removed.md` (the decisions) · `internal/alerts/service/sweep.go:717-745` (the retired `flap.score` sweep and \"RETIRED IN PLACE\") · `internal/alerts/repository/alert.go:1214-1235` (the deleted `SetFlap`), `:58-67` (why the columns stay in `alertColumns`), `:778` (the `?flapping=` filter) and `:996` (the rollup counter) · `internal/notification/domain/mode.go:166-178` (the clearest statement of what a reader now gets) · `internal/grouping/domain/lifecycle.go:51` and `internal/alerts/service/ports.go:61` (two more sites carrying the correct story) · SPEC §B.6.2.\n\n**Scope.** small. `00057` is applied and this repo does not edit an applied migration — `00036:99` invokes that rule for the same reason — so the fix is a `COMMENT ON COLUMN` on `alerts.flap_score` and `alerts.is_flapping` in a new migration, saying what they now hold.\n\n**Done when.** A new migration comments both columns as retired in place: last written by the deleted `flap.score` job, never recomputed, readable and stale, and supporting the words \"the last stored verdict\" rather than \"is flapping now\" — naming ADR 0041 Amendment 1 so the trail leads to the decision rather than to `00057`'s promise. `?flapping=` and the rollup's `flapping` counter are named as the two surfaces that serve the frozen value, so whoever next reads them knows what they are serving. The voided follow-up about a new `alert_events.type` is not left standing anywhere as live work.","files":null}]}